og `pid_state` (cross-track error)\n\nEnable bag recording of the CrabbingPathFollower's PID state, so the next mission captures **cross-track error + controller internals** (`control_msgs/PidState`: `error`=XTE, p/i/d terms, `output`=crab command). This is the missing data that would settle [#164](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/164) (SE-line undulation — high-gain limit-cycling vs. a disturbance the gains can't reject). The state publisher is **already live** (`activate_state_publisher: true` in the shared Nav2 config); it's just not in the recording list.\n\n- [ ] **Verify the exact topic name on the running stack** — do *not* guess; a wrong name silently records nothing (the same silent-failure class as #171/#162). On gabby with the nav stack up: `ros2 topic list | grep -i pid`. *(Source note: the follower builds `PidROS` with `topic_prefix=\"FollowPath/pid\"` — starts with an alphanumeric, so per control_toolbox `pid_ros.hpp` the topic is in the **global** namespace, i.e. ~`/FollowPath/pid/pid_state`, **not** under `/bizzy`. Confirm the precise string before editing.)*\n- [ ] Add the confirmed topic to the `/**/logger` → `record:` → `topics:` list in `bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat.yaml` (full path + one-line comment, matching the existing entries). Via issue → worktree → PR.\n- [ ] **In-deployment check:** once recording starts, confirm `pid_state` is actually present in the bag (`ros2 bag info`) — don't repeat the \"published-but-not-recorded\" gap.\n\n## 🔧 During deployment (opportunistic): operator annunciator coverage (#171)\n\nAdd **battery**, **FCU-system**, and **sound-speed** indicators to the operator annunciator (today it has only network/link rows), so the operator actually gets these warnings — gaps surfaced by the 2026-05-22 drain-to-LVD test ([#171](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/171)). Self-contained below so it works without GitHub access in the field (provenance / detail: [PR #180](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/180)). Best done live since the rows key on exact diagnostic strings.\n\n**1. Confirm exact strings on the live bus** (operator station, stack up) — don't guess; a wrong string silently matches nothing (same class as the `pid_state` task above):\n```bash\nros2 topic list | grep -i -E 'battery|diagnostic'\nros2 topic echo /diagnostics --once     # exact DiagnosticStatus.name + KeyValue keys\n```\n- [ ] `mavros: Battery` → exact **Voltage** KeyValue casing (on mismatch the row fails loud as `Voltage?`/ERROR, not silent green)\n- [ ] `mavros: System` status name (carries \"Battery N is low\" + FCU ERRORs; `mavros: Heartbeat` is already the boat \"FCU\" row)\n- [ ] the exact name `sound_speed_bridge` publishes — and that it publishes one at all (see #163); use `match_mode: substring` if it has a host/instance suffix\n- [ ] op-side **republished** name of `/bizzy/mavros/battery` — only needed for the topic-source battery fallback (step 3)\n\n**2. Append to `bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat_operator_annunciator.yaml`:**\n```yaml\n  # --- Boat health (forwarded over the link) ---\n  - name: Battery            # battery mechanism: see step 3\n    source: diagnostics\n    diagnostic_name: \"mavros: Battery\"\n    value_key: Voltage       # confirm casing live\n    format: \"{:.2f} V\"\n    thresholds:\n      warn: \"value \u003c 23.0\"   # FCU BATT_LOW_VOLT; tune vs Torqeedo Power 24-3500\n      error: \"value \u003c 21.5\"  # FCU BATT_CRT_VOLT\n  - name: FCU System\n    source: diagnostics\n    diagnostic_name: \"mavros: System\"\n    format: \"{}\"\n  - name: Sound Speed\n    source: diagnostics\n    diagnostic_name: \"sound_speed_bridge\"\n    match_mode: substring\n    format: \"{}\"\n    stale_timeout: 10.0\n```\n- [ ] Add the same `Sound Speed` row to `bizzyboat_annunciator.yaml` (boat side) — mind the overlap with [#179](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/179)'s battery-row edit (different rows, just merge-order).\n\n**3. Battery indicator — pick by what's deployed:**\n- If [rqt_operator_tools#36](https://github.com/rolker/rqt_operator_tools/pull/36) is deployed to the op station → use the `source: diagnostics` block above (consistent with the boat-side #162/#179 fix).\n- If **not** → fallback that works on the *current* engine (topic-source on the forwarded BatteryState):\n```yaml\n  - name: Battery\n    source: topic\n    topic: \u003cop-side republished /bizzy/mavros/battery\u003e   # confirm live (step 1)\n    msg_type: sensor_msgs/msg/BatteryState\n    value_field: voltage\n    format: \"{:.2f} V\"\n    thresholds:\n      warn: \"value \u003c 23.0\"\n      error: \"value \u003c 21.5\"\n```\nFCU-System and Sound-Speed have **no** #36 dependency either way.\n\n**4. Land it.** If the op-station checkout is gitcloud-origin → edit/commit/push in field mode, reconcile via `/import-field-changes` post-deployment. If GitHub-origin → normal worktree/PR.\n- [ ] Threshold values 23.0 / 21.5 (FCU params) — tune vs pack behavior if needed.\n\n## Standard deployment\n- [ ] Pre-deployment checklist (per the usual convention)\n- [ ] Per-host logs at `docs/logs/YYYY/YYYY-MM-DD_\u003chost\u003e_logs.md`\n- [ ] Wrap-up PR (`Closes #\u003cthis\u003e`)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":6,"timestamp":1779808531,"nonce":"OfV+hqSnC2TSVrqjGp6isGeGxMo=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lAHOK4fCvM8AAAABDVF0786-avAk"},"target":"20a49fcd9bd6820a06b2b4edc822b4ce59fc9283caa7f0c9406214e4d1805dca","message":"## Next BizzyBoat deployment\n\n\u003e **Set the date** in the title when scheduled (convention: `Deployment YYYY-MM-DD: …`). Created ahead of time to carry validation reminders for the turning-limit changes from [#124](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/124) §2.\n\n## ⚠️ Validate changed turning limits\n\nTwo limits changed since the last deployment — **both are field-untested**. Check