ker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/124)) under OTH load.\n\n## Standard deployment\n- [ ] Pre-deployment checklist (per the usual convention)\n- [ ] Per-host logs at `docs/logs/YYYY/YYYY-MM-DD_\u003chost\u003e_logs.md`\n- [ ] Wrap-up PR (`Closes #\u003cthis\u003e`)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":5,"timestamp":1779728190,"nonce":"vLZS96EgLK0ieZ/G7CgR7TP1Gsg=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDVF0788AAAAGCcspvw"},"added":["deployment"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779804896,"nonce":"P3ZFzPTszQ4zWBoY+hn8DqKGZ6U=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDuXuCw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/173#issuecomment-4544917003"},"message":"## Verify the reflex obstacle feed (perception#17 + Phase A)\n\nThe reflex `segments_to_pointcloud` adapter — PR rolker/unh_marine_perception#18 — is ready for review and now publishes **health diagnostics**. If it's running this deployment (merged to `jazzy` or built from the worktree), here's what's worth confirming in the field.\n\nPhase A (#178, merged) launches the reflex instance, remaps its output to `/bizzy/collision_monitor/pointcloud`, and records + bridges it. **Phase B** (rolker/seafloor_echoboat_project11#25 — the Collision Monitor *consuming* the cloud) is **not wired yet**, so unless #25 lands first this is a **feed-and-health test, not a \"does the boat stop\" test.**\n\n### Precondition\n- [ ] Reflex node is actually running — perception#17 provides the `target_frame` / `~/pointcloud` / diagnostics surface. Without it there's nothing to test.\n\n### Feed is alive (silent-failure class — same as the `pid_state` item above)\n- [ ] `/bizzy/collision_monitor/pointcloud` is publishing once the stack is up (`ros2 topic hz …`). Empty/absent = the LifecycleNode didn't configure→activate under its namespace (Phase A's load-bearing check) **or** no `camera_info` arrived.\n- [ ] Cloud `header.frame_id` is `bizzy/base_link_level`, not `map` (`ros2 topic echo --field header …`).\n\n### Health diagnostics (new this cycle — first field exercise)\n- [ ] The `/diagnostics` task **`obstacle projection feed`** reads **OK**, with `camera_info_received=true`, `clouds_published` climbing, `tf_lookup_failures`≈0, `nonfinite_points_dropped`≈0.\n- [ ] It surfaces on the operator annunciator (relates to the #171 annunciator-gap work). A WARN of `waiting for camera_info` or `projection failing (… TF for bizzy/base_link_level)` pinpoints the fault — confirm `mru_transform` is publishing `bizzy/base_link_level`.\n\n### Does it see real obstacles? (the actual point)\n- [ ] With a known object in the forward camera (mooring, dock, shoreline, another boat), obstacle points populate the **forward arc** of the cloud.\n- [ ] On open water with nothing ahead, the forward arc stays ~empty — **no phantom obstacles**. (The red-dominant segmentation heuristic is unchanged from the existing pipeline.)\n\n### Operator SA + cost\n- [ ] Operator station can view `/bizzy/collision_monitor/pointcloud` in rviz (Phase A bridges it on WiFi + VPN; measured \u003c2 KB/msg, negligible).\n- [ ] Point count per frame stays modest in cluttered scenes (shoreline fills the mask) — the node does **no range limiting**, so flag if density balloons or gabby CPU climbs. Spatial bounding is intentionally left to the Collision Monitor polygons (Phase B).\n\n### If Phase B (Collision Monitor wiring) lands before the deployment\n- [ ] The monitor's `pointcloud` observation source actually receives points — publisher QoS is **best-effort**; a *reliable* source gets nothing, silently.\n- [ ] The height window (`min_height`/`max_height`) includes the projected **z≈0** plane, or every point is filtered out.\n- [ ] Slow/limit behavior uses a standoff well beyond the ~10–15 m coast-down (#124 §2); favor slowdown over hard stop; forward arc only.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779807341,"nonce":"/sipn+W/8URpqwFKXjXsdMpKId0=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDuvjkg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/173#issuecomment-4545307538"},"message":"## Update — Phase B merged: now verify the Collision Monitor actually gates cmd_vel\n\nFollow-up to the \"Verify the reflex obstacle feed (perception#17 + Phase A)\" comment above. That comment's caveat — *\"Phase B … is not wired yet, so this is a feed-and-health test, not a 'does the boat stop' test\"* — **no longer holds**: Phase B (rolker/seafloor_echoboat_project11#25, PR rolker/seafloor_echoboat_project11#26) **merged to `jazzy` 2026-05-26 and is pushed to gitcloud**. The `collision_monitor` now consumes `/bizzy/collision_monitor/pointcloud`, replaces the old blind `scan` source, and runs momentum-tuned `CollisionSlowdown` (0–20 m) + `CollisionStop` (0–5 m) polygons on the autonomous `cmd_vel` path.\n\n**It merged un-sim-verified, with starting-value polygons** (user decision, same pattern as Phase A). So the \"does the boat stop\" test is now in scope — and sim verification is a hard gate before any autonomous run. The feed/health items in the comment above still apply as the precondition; the items below are the consumer side and are **not** duplicated there.\n\n### ⛔ Mandatory before any AUTONOMOUS run (sim first, per #170 scope)\n- [ ] **Sim**: with the reflex cloud injected/replayed, the monitor **slows** (to ~30% via `slowdown_ratio`) then **stops** `/bizzy/piloting_mode/autonomous/cmd_vel` when points fall in the forward danger sector — and **passes commands through unchanged when clear**.\n- [ ] **Sim**: the **manual RC-direct-to-FCU path is unaffected** — the monitor only gates the autonomous path; confirm a manual override still drives the boat with an obstacle present.\n- [ ] **`base_frame_id` resolves** — it was fixed from the wrong `base_footprint` to `\u003ctf_prefix\u003e/base_link`. Confirm the cloud (`bizzy/base_link_level`) TF-transforms into `bizzy/base_link` with no `collision_monitor` TF / \"source timed out\" warnings, and that the `min_height`/`max_height` (±2.0 m) bracket actually retains the projected points under realistic pitch (far points shift in z).\n\n### 🎛️ Tuning — starting values, NOT field-trusted\n- [ ] Polygon geometry (slowdown 0–20 m, stop 0–5 m), `slowdown_ratio` 0.3, and `min_points` (4/5) are **estimates**. Tune against sim + the Phase C offline trigger catalog (#169) before trusting on a mission.\n- [ ] **`min_points` direction is unresolved** — the two code reviewers split (too-high → misses small/distant obstacles vs too-low → nuisance stops on wake/shoreline at range). Watch for both failure modes; bias toward sensitivity since the motivating failure is **missed** obstacles.\n\n### 👁️ Observability during the run\n- [ ] `/bizzy/collision_monitor_state` transitions on detections (already in the bag `record:` list — confirm present via `ros2 bag info`, same silent-failure class as the `pid_state` item).\n- [ ] In sim/rviz, the polygon viz topics `/bizzy/collision_monitor/slowdown_polygon` + `/bizzy/collision_monitor/stop_polygon` (`visualize: true`) show the zones and light up on detections.\n\n### ⚠️ Known limitation (don't be surprised)\n- [ ] A **suddenly-appearing obstacle inside ~5 m** (sharp turn, sudden surfacing) still coasts ~10–15 m past a `stop` — inherent to passive braking with no reverse action (#88). Slowdown-first only protects when the obstacle is seen far out.\n\n\u003e Shared-config note: the Collision Monitor block lives in the seafloor `echoboat_project11` Nav2 params (shared with izzy). It's a no-op for izzy until izzy publishes the canonical topic, so this changes BizzyBoat behavior only.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779807615,"nonce":"X0LMWzUvQhK3/OfFln9Ndnx79bg=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDuyxvA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/173#issuecomment-4545360316"},"message":"Status update for the reflex-feed checks above: the perception adapter (rolker/unh_marine_perception#17) is **merged to `jazzy`** (PR #18, merge `401385c`). So the \"precondition\" box resolves to the *merged* path — the deployed bizzy stack just needs to **pull `jazzy` + rebuild the perception layer on gabby** to pick up reflex mode (`target_frame`) and the new `/diagnostics` health task. Until that pull/rebuild lands on gabby, the reflex node won't be present even though it's on `jazzy`.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779808862,"nonce":"BB6kCdTJMoumpblMb9IVjBIy154=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDu_bdQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/173#issuecomment-4545567605"},"message":"## Operator note — sim-verify is *not* a hard gate; `pid_state` is record-only\n\nTwo corrections from Roland (operator) on the reflex collision-avoidance items above:\n\n- **`pid_state` is record-only** — captured for post-deployment analysis, not a field-monitoring task. The only in-field check is that it actually lands in the bag.\n- **Sim-verification is not mandatory.** The \"⛔ Mandatory before any AUTONOMOUS run (sim first)\" framing in the comment above was an agent addition, not an operator decision, and is **overridden**. The emergency-stop / Collision Monitor behavior will be **baby-stepped on-water incrementally**. The feed/health and observability checks above remain useful as you go, but they are **not blocking**.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":2,"timestamp":1779809000,"nonce":"db27MhyLl2f02cBEApH/VnKMeIM=","metadata":{"github-id":"RTE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDVF0788AAAAGDCsQZA"},"title":"Deployment 2026-05-26: validate raised yaw cap (1.0) + planner radius (1.5)","was":"Deployment 2026-05-26: validate raised yaw cap (1.0) + planner radius (1.5)"}]}